tter approach: print the page 51 and 52 text fully (they're the last pages, maybe moderate) in this action along with the other verifications, then write in the next action. Page 51/52 text length maybe ~4000 chars each → 8000 chars output. Acceptable? Output budget... The instruction \"Do not print all pages\" — but 2 pages is fine. However, printed text also occupies my context of the response? It's tool output. Fine.\n\nLet's do: read pages 5,12,13,23,37,47,51,52; print targeted slices for 5,12,13,23,37,47 (short), and print full text of 51 and 52 (maybe truncated to needed parts). Then next action write report + pytest, next final_answer.\n\nWait — but that gives 3 actions: verify(1), write+test(2), final(3). requests_left 2 means 2 more after this one → total 3. Good.\n\nLet me write the code carefully with find and guards.\n\nCode:\n\n```python\npg = lambda a,b: read_pdf(a,b)['pages']\np5 = read_pdf(5,5)['pages'][0]['text']\n```\nCareful: read_pdf returns dict with 'pages'.\n\nLet me do:\n\n```python\ndef pgt(a,b):\n    return {p['page']:p['text'] for p in read_pdf(a,b)['pages']}\nt5 = read_pdf(5,5)['pages'][0]['text']\n...\n```\nMultiple calls fine.\n\nFor slices: define helper\n\n```python\ndef show(t, key, before=250, after=350):\n    i = t.find(key)\n    print('---', key, i)\n    if i>=0: print(repr(t[max(0,i-before):i+after]))\n```\n\nPrinting repr shows newlines exactly — useful.\n\nKeys: p5 'snowballing', p12 'majority', p13 'controller', p23 'calculator' and '16,464', p37 'inception', p47 '100 human', p51 'Training Data', p52 'self-verification'.\n\nAlso print full p51 and p52? Let me print p51 fully (needed for table) — use print(t51).\n\nHmm output size. Page text ~5000 chars → fine-ish.\n\nLet's include print of t51 entirely and slice of t52 around 'benefit'.\n\nGo."}, "logprobs": null, "finish_reason": "stop"}], "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 8585, "completion_tokens": 2966, "total_tokens": 11551, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 4224}, "comp